+---
+
+# Browser Sync Design
+
+## Context and Design Philosophy
+
+The browser sync component runs in each staff browser and maintains a live, revisioned view of the event board. It establishes a WebSocket connection to the delivery layer, handles reconnect with automatic catch-up, and presents a consistent board state to the UI. The design prioritizes visibility of connectivity state — browsers must never mistake a disconnected board for an unchanged one.
+
+## Connection Lifecycle
+
+### States
+
+| State | Description | UI Indicator |
+|-------|-------------|--------------|
+| `CONNECTING` | WebSocket handshake in progress | Spinner + "Connecting…" |
+| `SYNCED` | Connected, cursor = currentRevision | Green dot + "Live" |
+| `CATCHING_UP` | Replaying missed revisions after reconnect | Yellow dot + "Catching up (N revisions)…" |
+| `STALE` | Connected but cursor lags >5 revisions | Yellow dot + "Sync delayed" |
+| `DISCONNECTED` | No WebSocket connection; retry scheduled | Red dot + "Offline — retry in Ns" |
+| `ERROR` | Fatal error (auth, event ended) | Red banner + error message |
+
+### Transitions
+
+```
+CONNECTING → SYNCED (on WELCOME with cursor = currentRevision + 1)
+CONNECTING → CATCHING_UP (on WELCOME with boardSnapshot + cursor <= currentRevision)
+CONNECTING → ERROR (on ERROR frame or handshake failure)
+SYNCED → CATCHING_UP (on RESYNC response or proactive CATCH_UP)
+SYNCED → STALE (cursor lags >5 for >10s)
+SYNCED → DISCONNECTED (on close, timeout, or network error)
+CATCHING_UP → SYNCED (cursor catches up to currentRevision)
+CATCHING_UP → DISCONNECTED (on close/timeout during catch-up)
+DISCONNECTED → CONNECTING (after backoff, or on manual retry)
+DISCONNECTED → ERROR (on fatal error during reconnect)
+ERROR → (terminal; requires page reload or event change)
+```
+
+## WebSocket Client
+
+### Connection Parameters
+
+- URL: `wss://{host}/events/{eventId}/sync?cursor={cursor}`
+- `cursor` persisted in `sessionStorage` per event tab; survives tab reload
+- On first visit or explicit "fresh load", cursor omitted → full snapshot
+
+### Message Handler
+
+```
+on WELCOME:
+  - store sessionId
+  - if boardSnapshot present: applySnapshot(boardSnapshot)
+  - set cursor = welcome.cursor
+  - transition to SYNCED or CATCHING_UP
+
+on REVISION:
+  - if revision < cursor: ignore (duplicate)
+  - if revision == cursor: applyRevision(revision), cursor++
+  - if revision > cursor: gap detected → send RESYNC(cursor)
+
+on CATCH_UP:
+  - for each rev in revisions (in order):
+      if rev.revision >= cursor: applyRevision(rev), cursor = rev.revision + 1
+  - transition to SYNCED
+
+on HEARTBEAT:
+  - send PING { clientTime: now() }
+  - update lastHeartbeatAt
+
+on ERROR:
+  - if retryable: transition to DISCONNECTED
+  - else: transition to ERROR
+
+on GOODBYE:
+  - transition to DISCONNECTED
+```
+
+### Heartbeat & Timeout
+
+- Server sends HEARTBEAT every 15s
+- Client must send PING within 5s of HEARTBEAT receipt
+- If no HEARTBEAT received for 25s (15s interval + 5s grace + 5s margin), assume connection dead → transition to DISCONNECTED
+- Client sends PING proactively every 10s as additional liveness signal
+
+## Reconnect Strategy
+
+### Backoff Schedule
+
+| Attempt | Delay | Jitter |
+|---------|-------|--------|
+| 1 | 1 s | ±200 ms |
+| 2 | 2 s | ±400 ms |
+| 3 | 4 s | ±800 ms |
+| 4 | 8 s | ±1.6 s |
+| 5+ | 15 s | ±3 s |
+
+Max 5 rapid retries, then 15s steady interval. Cap at 20 minutes (goal: recover after 20 min disconnect).
+
+### Reconnect Procedure
+
+1. Enter `DISCONNECTED` state, schedule retry per backoff
+2. On retry: read persisted `cursor` from `sessionStorage`
+3. Open WebSocket with `?cursor={cursor}`
+4. On WELCOME:
+   - If `boardSnapshot` present: full reset → applySnapshot, set cursor
+   - Else if `cursor` matches server's `cursor`: seamless resume
+   - Else: gap → will receive CATCH_UP or REVISION gap triggers RESYNC
+5. Persist new `cursor` on each successful revision apply
+
+### Cursor Persistence
+
+- Key: `marketboard:cursor:{eventId}`
+- Value: `{ revision: number, timestamp: ISO8601 }`
+- Updated on every successful revision apply
+- Cleared on explicit "clear board" or event change
+
+## Board State Management
+
+### State Representation
+
+```typescript
+interface BoardState {
+  stalls: Map<StallId, StallStatus>;
+  revision: number;
+  lastUpdate: Date;
+}
+
+type StallStatus = 
+  | { state: 'OPEN' }
+  | { state: 'CLOSED'; reason: string; at: Date }
+  | { state: 'POWER_ISSUE'; detail: string; at: Date }
+  | { state: 'LATE'; expectedAt: Date }
+  | { state: 'UNKNOWN' };
+```
+
+### Applying Revisions
+
+- `applySnapshot(snapshot)`: Replaces entire `stalls` map, sets `revision = snapshot.revision`
+- `applyRevision(rev)`: Mutates single stall per `rev.command`, increments `revision`
+- Both are synchronous, pure functions — easy to test and reason about
+
+### UI Subscription
+
+React components (or equivalent) subscribe via a selector hook:
+
+```typescript
+function useStallStatus(eventId: string, stallId: string): StallStatus | null
+function useBoardSnapshot(eventId: string): BoardState | null
+function useSyncState(eventId: string): SyncState
+```
+
+Selectors compute derived state from the normalized `BoardState` — no redundant stores.
+
+## Offline & Tab Lifecycle
+
+### Page Visibility
+
+- Tab hidden: continue WebSocket (browser throttles timers but WS stays alive)
+- Tab visible after hidden: send `PING` immediately to verify liveness
+- If `lastHeartbeatAt > 30s ago`: force reconnect
+
+### Browser Sleep/Wake
+
+- On wake: `visibilitychange` fires → same as tab visible logic
+- If disconnect > 20 min: cursor may be stale beyond retention → WELCOME returns full snapshot
+
+### Service Worker (Non-Goal)
+
+- Offline editing is a non-goal
+- No service worker for pilot; plain WebSocket + sessionStorage suffices
+
+## Error Handling
+
+### Recoverable Errors
+
+| Code | Cause | Action |
+|------|-------|--------|
+| `CAPACITY` | Server at session limit | Backoff retry |
+| `STALE_CURSOR` | Cursor too old, full snapshot sent | Apply snapshot, continue |
+| `HEARTBEAT_TIMEOUT` | No HEARTBEAT for 25s | Reconnect |
+
+### Fatal Errors
+
+| Code | Cause | Action |
+|------|-------|--------|
+| `UNAUTHORIZED` | Session expired or role revoked | Redirect to sign-in |
+| `EVENT_ENDED` | Event no longer published | Show "Event ended" banner |
+| `PROTOCOL_ERROR` | Frame parse failure | Reload page |
+
+### Visibility Rule
+
+Per tenet: *Connectivity failures must be visible, not mistaken for an unchanged board.* The `SyncState` is always reflected in the UI — at minimum a colored indicator dot in the header, with tooltip detail on hover.
+
+## Decisions & Alternatives
+
+| Decision | Chosen | Alternatives Considered | Rationale |
+|----------|--------|------------------------|-----------|
+| Cursor persistence | `sessionStorage` per tab | `localStorage`; IndexedDB; in-memory only | `sessionStorage` survives reload, isolates tabs (multi-tab editing), clears on browser close — matches coordinator workflow |
+| Reconnect backoff | Exponential with jitter, cap at 15s | Fixed interval; linear backoff; no cap | Exponential avoids thundering herd; cap bounds worst-case recovery; jitter desynchronizes mass reconnect |
+| Gap detection | Client sends RESYNC on revision gap | Server pushes CATCH_UP proactively always; client polls REST | Client-driven RESYNC is simple, puts control in browser, works with any server implementation |
+| State mutation | Synchronous pure functions on revision apply | Immutable Redux-style; Observable streams | Pure functions are testable, no framework lock-in, trivial to port |
+| UI sync indicator | Required per tenet | Optional; hidden in menu | Tenet mandates visibility; indicator dot is minimal, always present |
+
+## Open Questions & Future Decisions
+
+### Resolved
+1. ✅ Self-hosted WebSockets — browser implements reconnect/catch-up per delivery protocol
+
+### Deferred
+1. Multi-tab coordination (shared worker for single connection across tabs) — pilot uses per-tab connection
+2. Background tab throttling mitigation (Page Visibility API + explicit wake check)
+3. Revision compression for catch-up batches >100 (delta encoding vs full snapshots)
+4. Metrics: client-side latency histogram (server timestamp → client apply)
+5. Accessibility: screen-reader announcements for sync state changes
+
+## References
+
+- High-Level Design: `docs/high-level-design.md`
+- Delivery Design: `docs/intent/delivery/delivery-design.md` (protocol definition)
+- Change Store Design: `docs/intent/change-store/change-store-design.md` (revision model)
+- Access Design: `docs/intent/access/access-design.md` (authorization context)
