+# Browser Sync Specifications
+
+- [ ] **BROWSER-001**: When the browser loads an event board, the system shall open a WebSocket connection to the delivery endpoint with the persisted cursor from sessionStorage (if any).
+- [ ] **BROWSER-002**: When a WELCOME frame with boardSnapshot is received, the system shall apply the snapshot as the current board state and set cursor to welcome.cursor.
+- [ ] **BROWSER-003**: When a REVISION frame is received with revision == cursor, the system shall apply the revision to the board state and increment cursor.
+- [ ] **BROWSER-004**: When a REVISION frame is received with revision > cursor, the system shall send a RESYNC frame with the current cursor to request catch-up.
+- [ ] **BROWSER-005**: When a CATCH_UP frame is received, the system shall apply each revision in order where revision >= cursor, updating cursor to the last applied revision + 1.
+- [ ] **BROWSER-006**: The system shall send a PING response within 5 seconds of receiving a HEARTBEAT frame.
+- [ ] **BROWSER-007**: If no HEARTBEAT is received for 25 seconds, the system shall treat the connection as dead and initiate reconnect.
+- [ ] **BROWSER-008**: When the WebSocket closes or times out, the system shall transition to DISCONNECTED state and schedule a reconnect with exponential backoff (1s, 2s, 4s, 8s, 15s capped, ±20% jitter).
+- [ ] **BROWSER-009**: On reconnect, the system shall open a new WebSocket with the persisted cursor from sessionStorage.
+- [ ] **BROWSER-010**: The system shall persist the cursor to sessionStorage on every successful revision apply.
+- [ ] **BROWSER-011**: The system shall expose a sync state (CONNECTING, SYNCED, CATCHING_UP, STALE, DISCONNECTED, ERROR) that is always reflected in the UI.
+- [ ] **BROWSER-012**: If the server returns ERROR { retryable: false } or GOODBYE with a fatal reason, the system shall transition to ERROR state and not attempt reconnect.
+- [ ] **BROWSER-013**: When the tab becomes visible after being hidden, if the last HEARTBEAT was received more than 30 seconds ago, the system shall force a reconnect.
+- [ ] **BROWSER-014**: The system shall apply revisions and snapshots via pure synchronous functions that take the previous board state and return the new board state.
+- [ ] **BROWSER-015**: The system shall recover the latest board after a disconnect of up to 20 minutes by reconnecting and replaying missed revisions (or receiving a full snapshot if cursor is beyond retention).
