+# Change Store Specifications
+
+- [ ] **CHANGE-001**: When a command handler commits an edit for an event, the system shall assign the next sequential revision number for that event and persist the revision with the command, actor ID, timestamp, and full board snapshot.
+- [ ] **CHANGE-002**: When a revision is committed, the system shall write a corresponding publication outbox row in the same database transaction.
+- [ ] **CHANGE-003**: The system shall provide a full board snapshot by returning the board_snapshot_json from the latest revision for an event.
+- [ ] **CHANGE-004**: When a browser requests revisions since a cursor, the system shall return all revisions for that event where revision > cursor, ordered by revision ascending.
+- [ ] **CHANGE-005**: The system shall retain revisions for at least seven days for operational investigation.
+- [ ] **CHANGE-006**: If a commit transaction fails, the system shall return an error to the command handler and create no revision or outbox row.
+- [ ] **CHANGE-007**: The system shall support 20 edits per second burst writes for a single event without blocking readers.
+- [ ] **CHANGE-008**: While an archive job runs, the system shall not block revision commits or delivery reads.
